// vision.marco — the Vision act surface: SEMANTIC on-screen UI-element detection,
// fulfilled by the resolver plugin (see plugins/vision). Imported by routes with
// `use vision.`. Where image/colour/edge anchors are GEOMETRIC and Text is OCR, Vision is
// a learned detector: it finds buttons, icons, menu items and prompts — including controls
// with no clean edges (an icon on a gradient) — and labels each by KIND. With no
// `--host Vision=bridge:vision` wired (or no model loaded), Locate/Detect resolve failed
// and the route falls back to its recorded coordinate or another resolver — purely additive.

the Vision is an act.
this exports Detect.    // all elements: { X1?,Y1?,X2?,Y2? } -> { Elements }  (each { Label, X, Y, W, H, Score })
this exports Locate.    // best element -> Point: { Label?, X?,Y? hint, X1?,Y1?,X2?,Y2? } -> { X, Y }

// Locate returns an { X, Y } point in absolute screen coordinates — the same shape OS's
// Click/Move and Text's Find accept — so it drops into the same resolver slot. The Point
// type itself comes from os.marco (every route that uses Vision also `use os.`), so it
// isn't redeclared here.
